(This comprehensive note set explores the rigorous mathematical foundations of quantum mechanics, tailored for) Tj
T* (PhD-level researchers. We traverse the algebraic structure of quantum theory, commencing with the formulation of) Tj
T* (states and observables within the framework of Hilbert spaces and self-adjoint operators. Key topics include the) Tj
T* (spectral theorem, density operator formalism, time-evolution pictures, and the Feynman path integral formulation.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Additionally, we delve into the topological and group-theoretic underpinnings of quantum mechanics, emphasizing) Tj
T* (Wigner's theorem, Lie groups, and Lie algebras in relation to spatial symmetries and spin. This document serves as) Tj
T* (both an analytical reference and an advanced study guide for researchers seeking a mathematically uncompromising) Tj
T* (view of quantum systems.) Tj
