40. 394.8899999999999864 Td
(Q3. Explain how the interaction picture simplifies the calculation of scattering amplitudes in quantum field theory.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
50. 376.8899999999999864 Td
(Ans: In quantum field theory, the total Hamiltonian H is usually split into a solvable free-field part H_0 and a complex interaction) Tj
T* (part V. ) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (In the Interaction \(Dirac\) Picture:) Tj
T* (1. The operators evolve according to H_0: A_I\(t\) = e^\(i H_0 t/hbar\) A_S e^\(-i H_0 t/hbar\). This evolution is usually easy to) Tj
T* (compute because H_0 is quadratic in fields.) Tj
T* (2. The state vectors evolve according to V_I\(t\): ihbar \(d\)/\(dt\)|psi_I\(t\)> = V_I\(t\)|psi_I\(t\)>.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (This separation allows us to isolate the complex physical interactions into the state evolution, which can be solved) Tj
T* (perturbatively using the Dyson series expansion of the time-evolution operator U_I\(t, t_0\):) Tj
T* (\\) Tj
T* (U_I\(t, t_0\) = I + sum_\(n=1\)^\(infinity\) \(-\(i\)/\(hbar\)\)^n integral_\(t_0\)^t dt_1 integral_\(t_0\)^\(t_1\) dt_2 ... integral_\(t_0\)^\(t_\(n-1\)\) dt_n) Tj
T* (V_I\(t_1\)dotsV_I\(t_n\) \\) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (This formulation is the foundation of Feynman diagrams and the calculation of S-matrix elements.) Tj
ET
BT
/F2 9.5 Tf
10.9249999999999989 TL
0.059 0.09 0.165 rg
40. 186.8899999999999864 Td
(Q4. Demonstrate the mathematical steps to transition from the path integral formulation to the time-dependent) Tj
T* (Schrdinger equation.) Tj
