/F1 9 Tf
10.3499999999999996 TL
0.2 0.255 0.333 rg
50. 796.8899999999999864 Td
(Ans: To derive the Schrdinger equation, consider the propagator over an infinitesimal time step epsilon:) Tj
T* (\\) Tj
T* (psi\(x, t+epsilon\) = integral_\(-infinity\)^\(infinity\) K\(x, t+epsilon; x', t\) psi\(x', t\) dx' \\) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Using the path integral propagator for a short time step epsilon:) Tj
T* (\\) Tj
T* (K\(x, t+epsilon; x', t\) ~= sqrt\(\(m\)/\(2pi i hbar epsilon\)\) exp\( \(i\)/\(hbar\) [ \(m\(x-x'\)^2\)/\(2epsilon\) - epsilon V\(\(x+x'\)/\(2\), t\) ] \) \\) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Let eta = x' - x. Then x' = x + eta. Substitute this into the integral:) Tj
T* (\\) Tj
T* (psi\(x, t+epsilon\) = sqrt\(\(m\)/\(2pi i hbar epsilon\)\) integral_\(-infinity\)^\(infinity\) exp\( \(imeta^2\)/\(2hbarepsilon\) \) exp\( -\(iepsilon\)/\(hbar\)) Tj
T* (V\(x + \(eta\)/\(2\), t\) \) psi\(x+eta, t\) deta \\) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Because of the highly oscillating term exp\(imeta^2/2hbarepsilon\), the integral only gets non-vanishing contributions when eta is) Tj
T* (very small \(order of sqrt\(hbarepsilon/m\)\). We expand psi\(x+eta, t\) and V\(x+eta/2\) as a Taylor series in powers of eta and) Tj
T* (epsilon:) Tj
T* (- psi\(x+eta, t\) ~= psi\(x,t\) + eta \(d psi\)/\(d x\) + \(eta^2\)/\(2\) \(d^2 psi\)/\(d x^2\)) Tj
T* (- exp\(-\(iepsilon\)/\(hbar\) V\) ~= 1 - \(iepsilon\)/\(hbar\) V\(x, t\)) Tj
T* (- psi\(x, t+epsilon\) ~= psi\(x, t\) + epsilon \(d psi\)/\(d t\)) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Using standard Gaussian integrals:) Tj
T* (- integral_\(-infinity\)^\(infinity\) exp\(iaeta^2\) deta = sqrt\(\(ipi\)/\(a\)\)) Tj
T* (- integral_\(-infinity\)^\(infinity\) eta exp\(iaeta^2\) deta = 0) Tj
T* (- integral_\(-infinity\)^\(infinity\) eta^2 exp\(iaeta^2\) deta = \(i\)/\(2a\)sqrt\(\(ipi\)/\(a\)\)) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (We substitute these results back and simplify. The leading order terms cancel, and matching the first-order terms in epsilon) Tj
T* (yields:) Tj
T* (\\) Tj
T* (epsilon \(d psi\)/\(d t\) = -\(iepsilon\)/\(hbar\) V\(x, t\) psi\(x, t\) + \(ihbarepsilon\)/\(2m\) \(d^2 psi\)/\(d x^2\) \\) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Multiplying both sides by ihbar/epsilon yields the Schrdinger Equation:) Tj
T* (\\) Tj
T* (ihbar \(d psi\)/\(d t\) = -\(hbar^2\)/\(2m\) \(d^2 psi\)/\(d x^2\) + V\(x, t\)psi\(x, t\) \\) Tj
